From: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
Date: Thu, 08 Oct 2026 17:47:01 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] AP: Clear authorized flag when re-adding a STA to the driver

When an associated STA sends a new (Re)Association Request frame, the
AP can remove the STA entry from the driver and add it again. The
removal deletes the pairwise key, but the STA keeps its authorized
flag, so the new driver entry is authorized and has no key. Until the
4-way handshake or the FT key installation completes, the driver can
send unicast data frames to the STA without encryption.

Clear the authorized flag together with the removal. The new driver
entry is then unauthorized, and the driver sends no unicast data to it
until the handshake or the FT reassociation sets the flag again. The
STA stays associated, so no AP-STA-DISCONNECTED event is sent; a
control interface monitor sees a second AP-STA-CONNECTED event when
the flag is set again.

The change comes from mtk-openwrt-feeds 2df62b873dd2 ("[openwrt-25]
[MAC80211][WiFi7][kernel 6.12][Prepare for Filogic 880/850 Alpha
release]").

Co-developed-by: Michael-CY Lee <michael-cy.lee@mediatek.com>
Signed-off-by: Michael-CY Lee <michael-cy.lee@mediatek.com>
Signed-off-by: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
---
 src/ap/ieee802_11.c |    6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

--- a/src/ap/ieee802_11.c
+++ b/src/ap/ieee802_11.c
@@ -6711,6 +6711,12 @@ static int add_associated_sta(struct hos
 		hostapd_drv_sta_remove(hapd, sta->addr);
 		wpa_auth_sm_event(sta->wpa_sm, WPA_DRV_STA_REMOVED);
 		set = 0;
+		/*
+		 * The new driver entry has no key until the 4-way handshake or
+		 * the FT key installation. Clear the flag without an event,
+		 * because the STA stays associated.
+		 */
+		ap_sta_set_authorized_flag(hapd, sta, 0);
 
 		 /* Do not allow the FT-over-DS exception to be used more than
 		  * once per authentication exchange to guarantee a new TK is
